@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "SMSer — group texts, easier";
}

<div class="hero">
    <h1>Group texts, easier.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
        Paste a roster — however garbled it came off your phone — and get back a link
        and a QR code that open a group message with everyone already in it.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-large" href="/new">Start a new list</a>
        <span class="hero-aside">takes about a minute</span>
    </div>
</div>

@*
    The step numerals are decorative — the headings already carry the order, and reading
    "one" before "Paste anything" adds nothing.
*@
<div class="cards">
    <section class="card">
        <p class="card-step" aria-hidden="true">1</p>
        <h2>Paste anything</h2>
        <p>
            Names, jersey numbers, e-mail addresses, whatever the camera's "copy as text"
            produced. The importer finds the phone numbers in it and ignores the rest.
        </p>
    </section>
    <section class="card">
        <p class="card-step" aria-hidden="true">2</p>
        <h2>Scan or tap</h2>
        <p>
            Scan the QR code with a phone, or tap the mobile link, and the messaging app
            opens with the whole list in the To: field.
        </p>
    </section>
    <section class="card">
        <p class="card-step" aria-hidden="true">3</p>
        <h2>Keep the link</h2>
        <p>
            Every list gets its own short URL. Come back to it next season, fix a number,
            and regenerate — the link stays the same.
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
